  "notes": [
    "Static art for card mini-games: one shared back, five face templates and four suit symbols. Nothing here is an animation.",
    "A playing card is assembled by the game: a face template, the rank and suit drawn into the two index areas, and for the ace and 2 to 10 the suit symbols placed at the pip centres.",
    "The index areas are blank parchment on every face template. No ranks, numbers or fonts are in the image.",
    "Stamp a suit from its 'crop' (the same 96 x 96 area in every suit cell) so the four symbols keep their relative sizes; 'bounds' is the exact painted area.",
    "The back, plain face and the three court cards look the same upside down; the joker does not.",
    "A flip is shown by squeezing the card to nothing across its width over half of flipMs, swapping the side, and widening again.",
    "The three decks are skins of one layout: the back, plain face and four suits are the same pixels in each, and only the joker, king, queen and jack pictures differ. A game can swap decks by swapping the image."
  ]
